{
  "id": "COMPOUND:14789 - PROTEIN:737",
  "verbalization": "Insulin is linked to the Sodium-dependent proline transporter through a series of molecular interactions involving Cyclin-dependent kinase 7 (CDK7). CDK7 is a target of multiple compounds, including (2R,3S,4S,5R,6R)-2-[[(2R,3R,4R,5S)-3,4-dihydroxy-5-(hydroxymethyl)oxolan-2-yl]oxymethyl]-6-[(2Z)-3,7-dimethylocta-2,6-dienoxy]oxane-3,4,5-triol, Bakuchalcone, and (+)-Parviflorol. These compounds all act as inhibitors of the Sodium-dependent proline transporter, suggesting a common mechanism of action. The evidence supports a direct interaction between insulin and the transporter, mediated through CDK7, which is a key regulator of cellular processes. The high scores in the paths indicate a strong, consistent relationship, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact nature of the interaction. The presence of multiple compounds targeting the same pathway strengthens the hypothesis, but the integration of these findings into a unified mechanism requires additional biochemical and pharmacological data.",
